      <sectiondef kind="func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="xpm__abist_8c_1a3abf7d159f82fb4b49a844605b9d2fbb" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>XStatus</type>
        <definition>XStatus XPmPl_Abist</definition>
        <argsstring>(u32 DomainMask)</argsstring>
        <name>XPmPl_Abist</name>
        <param>
          <type>u32</type>
          <declname>DomainMask</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Runs Arteris built-in self-test (ABIST) for PL-related LPD, FPD, and ASU Domains. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Tests only the selected LPD AFIFS, FPD AFIFS, and INTASU PL controllers whose base-register reads are nonzero. Each ABIST is only required to execute once after booting. Skips testing on QEMU and COSIM platforms or when housecleaning disables PLD ABIST.</para><para>Temporarily enables the RCLK clock outputs and restores CRP_RCLK_CTRL before returning. For each tested controller, disables interrupts, starts BIST, polls for completion, and checks for a latent fault. Clears BIST completion and polls for mission mode before recording successful completion. Subsequent calls skip controllers already marked complete.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>DomainMask</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>OR of XPM_ABIST_LPD_MASK, XPM_ABIST_FPD_MASK, and XPM_ABIST_ASU_MASK. Zero selects no controllers.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS if all attempted tests succeed or no test runs.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_INVALID_PARAM for unsupported DomainMask bits.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE if a latent fault is detected.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Polling failure status if BIST completion or mission-mode polling fails.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>A zero base-register read leaves that controller eligible for a subsequent call. Success does not imply every controller completed ABIST. Completion flags persist across calls until software reinitializes them. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
